      ":question/id": "6314fa47-1361-54c0-9592-6cc5e58452ed",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=31^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 31^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(62^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
